Chapter: AhciEncode
  cites Works chapter GopAhci

 Known-answer checks for the AHCI structures the HBA reads by DMA. A
 wrong byte here is a wrong command issued to real hardware, and the
 controller is under no obligation to complain -- it will happily read
 the wrong sector into the wrong place. So the command header, the
 register host-to-device FIS, and the PRDT entry are all built into a
 scratch buffer and compared against the values the AHCI 1.3.1
 specification and the ATA command set require.

 The LBA under test is 0x0102030405 -- every LBA byte distinct, so a
 transposed field cannot pass.

Section: Main

  hex-digit : Integer -> Text
  hex-digit (v) =
    if v == 0 then "0" else if v == 1 then "1" else if v == 2 then "2"
    else if v == 3 then "3" else if v == 4 then "4" else if v == 5 then "5"
    else if v == 6 then "6" else if v == 7 then "7" else if v == 8 then "8"
    else if v == 9 then "9" else if v == 10 then "a" else if v == 11 then "b"
    else if v == 12 then "c" else if v == 13 then "d" else if v == 14 then "e"
    else "f"

  hex32 : Integer -> Text
  hex32 (v) = hex-nib v 7

  hex-nib : Integer, Integer -> Text
  hex-nib (v) (i) =
    if i < 0 then ""
    else hex-digit (bit-and (bit-shru v (i * 4)) 15) & hex-nib v (i - 1)

  test-lba : Integer = 4328719365

 Each check takes the buffer as a parameter. A zero-argument `scratch`
 def would NOT do: a nullary def is re-evaluated at every mention, so
 `alloc-zeroed` would hand each read a fresh, freshly-zeroed buffer and
 every check would pass by reading its own zeros.

 The FIS: dword 0 is type 0x27 (H2D), the command bit, command 0x25
 (READ DMA EXT). Dword 1 carries LBA bytes 0..2 and device 0x40 (LBA
 mode). Dword 2 carries LBA bytes 3..5. Dword 3 is a sector count of 1.

  fis-check : Integer -> Text
  fis-check (buf) =
    let w = ahci-write-fis buf test-lba
    in "fis0=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 0)
     & " fis1=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 4)
     & " fis2=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 8)
     & " fis3=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 12)

  header-check : Integer -> Text
  header-check (buf) =
    let w = ahci-write-header buf 305419896
    in "hdr0=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 0) & " ctba=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 8)

  prdt-check : Integer -> Text
  prdt-check (buf) =
    let w = ahci-write-prdt buf 2864434397
    in "dba=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 128) & " dbc=" & hex32 (peek-32 buf 140)

  bits-check : Text
  bits-check =
    "clear-set=" & show (clear-bit 5 1)
    & " clear-unset=" & show (clear-bit 4 1)
    & " align1024=" & show (align-up 1 1024)
    & " align-exact=" & show (align-up 2048 1024)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (header-check (alloc-zeroed 512 128))
    print-line-uni (fis-check (alloc-zeroed 512 128))
    print-line-uni (prdt-check (alloc-zeroed 512 128))
    print-line-uni bits-check
  end
